r cadence is only ~1 per 5-min when the backfill reconciler is the sole driver, and that rate is not robust to a single empty alarm period.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe8bf3e19d05e6b00","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Why 3-of-3', bullet 'The discriminator is PERSISTENCE ... so an outage breaches every consecutive period'; and AC line 1","norm_id":"n25efe2e396390183","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Expired bot token during a quiet window: no live webhook traffic, only the 5-min reconciler re-drives vote-less changes, ~1 VOTER_ERROR per pass; a boundary-straddling or missing-datapoint period breaks the 3-of-3 streak and the stuck gate does not page within 15 min","LLM outage overnight with low change volume: reconciler-only markers at ~5-min cadence intermittently skip a period, delaying or preventing the page the ruling requires"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add grounding that the busy-system assumption holds, or size the alarm to tolerate one gap: evaluate whether the sustained-marker cadence during a reconciler-only outage reliably exceeds one per period; if not, revise the shape to N-of-M consecutive-window (e.g. 4-of-5 x 300s, still ≤~25 min) which pages on a slow sustained stream while an isolated transient still breaches ≤2 datapoints.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":